 editor</nobr></h1><ul id="giftools-menu"><li class="video-to-gif"><a href="/video-to-gif" title="Video to GIF online converter">Video to GIF</a><li class="gif-maker"><a href="/maker" title="Make animated GIF from multiple images">GIF Maker</a><li class="resize"><a href="/resize" title="Resize GIFs and other animated images">Resizer</a><li class="optimizer"><a href="/optimize" title="Optimize animated GIFs for file size and performance">Optimizer</a></ul><p id="site-description">Ezgif.com is a simple, free online GIF maker and toolset for basic animated image
editing.<br>Here you can create, edit and convert GIF, APNG, WebP, MNG, JXL and AVIF animations.<div id="news"><h2>ezgif.com news and updates</h2><ul><li><span class="date">Oct 16, 2026</span><p>Many converters on the site, e.g. <a href="/webp-to-jpg">WebP to JPG</a> and <a href="/png-to-jpg">PNG to JPG</a>, now support batch mode client side processing by default. It means that you can upload multiple files at once and they will be processed directly in your browser without being uploaded to Ezgif's servers. If you prefer the old server-side processing workflow, you can still switch to it using the mode switch above the upload form.<li><span class="date">Oct 14, 2026</span><p>Some tools (e.g., <a href="/video-to-gif">Video to GIF</a>) now feature a <em>Local processing</em> checkbox. When selected, files are processed directly in your browser without being uploaded to Ezgif's servers. In local mode, there are no file size limits, no waiting for uploads, and you can rest assured that your files remain private. Not all tools and formats are supported yet, but basic GIF editing tasks should work.<li><span class="date">Oct 11, 2026</span><p>Added a new tool in video section: <a href="/video-mixer">Online Video Mixer & Multi-Track Timeline Editor</a>. You can combine and edit multiple video, GIF and audio tracks on an interactive timeline with visual trimming, splitting, and drag-and-drop sequencing. It supports picture-in-picture overlays, independent volume controls, transition effects between clips (crossfade, wipe, slide, iris, dissolve), and export presets for Full HD, Square, and Vertical video formats. After the files are uploaded you can always switch between the new video mixer and the old <a href="/merge-videos">Video Merge</a> tool.<li><span class="date">Aug 30, 2026</span><p>All animation maker tools (<a href="/webp-maker">WebP Maker</a>, <a href="/apng-maker">APNG Maker</a>, <a href="/avif-maker">AVIF Maker</a>, <a href="/jxl-maker">JXL Maker</a>, and <a href="/mng-maker">MNG Maker</a>) now support combining images of different sizes, custom per-frame offsets, and gravity alignment options (previously only available in the <a href="/maker">GIF Maker</a>).<li><span class="date">Aug 22, 2026</span><p>Added a new tool: <a href="/screen-recorder">Online Screen Recorder</a>. You can record your screen, window, or browser tab directly in your browser with customizable quality settings (up to 4K/30fps), and then edit and convert the recording to GIF, WebP, APNG, MP4 or save the video directly.<p>Added a new <a href="/target-size-compressor">GIF Target Size Compressor</a> for automatically optimizing GIFs to fit target file size limits (256 KB, 128 KB, 10 MB, etc.) for Discord, Slack, email, or web uploads.<p>Introduced a client-side <a href="/gif-batch-optimizer">Bulk GIF Optimizer</a> powered by WebAssembly (gifsicle WASM) for compressing multiple GIF files at once directly in your browser without uploads, with lossy compression support and single-click ZIP downloads.<p>Also added support for Lottie animation files (.json and .lottie) with <a href="/lottie-to-gif">Lottie to GIF</a>, <a href="/lottie-to-webp">Lottie to WebP</a>, and <a href="/lottie-to-apng">Lottie to APNG</a> converters, and Aseprite files (.ase and .aseprite) with <a href="/aseprite-to-gif">Aseprite to GIF</a>, <a href="/aseprite-to-webp">Aseprite to WebP</a>, and <a href="/aseprite-to-apng">Aseprite to APNG</a> converters and <a href="/maker">GIF Maker</a> support.<li><span class="date">Aug 4, 2026</span><p>Improved support for Windows Animated Cursors (.ani). You can now convert <a href="/gif-to-ani">GIF to ANI</a>, as well as <a href="/ani-to-gif">convert ANI to GIF</a>, WebP, or APNG, split ANI files into individual frames, and edit ANI cursors using crop, resize, rotate tools.<li><span class="date">Jul 28, 2026</span><p>The <a href="/cut-video">Video Cutter</a> now features an interactive timeline with thumbnail previews. When you change the start or end time, thumbnails at the exact positions are generated dynamically, making it easier to find the precise cut points. It also now allows inverting the selection (cut out a part of the video and splice the remaining parts together) (<a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/ezgif/comments/1v2tak3/two_suggestions_for_online_video_cutter_trimmer/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" class="external">discussion</a>).<li><span class="date">Jun 25, 2026</span><p>Expanded the audio tools with new utilities:<p><ul><li><a href="/compress-audio">Audio Compressor</a> for reducing file sizes by adjusting bitrate, sample rate, and channels.<li><a href="/audio-fade">Fade In/Out</a> editor with multiple curve types for smooth audio transitions.<li><a href="/audio-waveform">Waveform Generator</a> that creates customizable waveform images from audio files.<li><a href="/audio-speed">Audio Speed Changer</a> with optional pitch preservation for speeding up or slowing down audio.</ul><p>All tools support MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A, and OGG formats.<li><span class="date">Jun 24, 2026</span><p>Added new converters for less common/legacy animation formats: <a href="/flif-to-gif">FLIF to GIF</a>, <a href="/flif-to-png">FLIF to PNG</a>, <a href="/bpg-to-gif">BPG to GIF</a>, <a href="/fli-to-png">FLI to PNG</a>, <a href="/cdxl-to-gif">CDXL to GIF</a>, and <a href="/cdxl-to-png">CDXL to PNG</a>. Also expanded support for FLIF, BPG, FLI/FLC, Amiga ANIM, and Amiga CDXL files across the splitter and maker tools.<li><span class="date">May 31, 2026</span><p>The <a href="/white-box-caption">white box caption</a> tool now supports video files in addition to animated images. You can add iFunny-style top or bottom captions to MP4, WebM, MOV and other video formats (<a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/ezgif/comments/1tsuy6t/is_there_a_way_for_me_to_add_this_to_mp4s_instead/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" class="external">discussion</a>).</ul><p class="paginator"><a href="/" class="active">1</a> <a href="/archive/2">2</a> 